course: dictionary
lesson: 1422
title: Words in brackets
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Sometimes an author explains a hard word straight away, in brackets. Look out for this clue. «Tooth decay (dentists call it caries) is the most common long-lasting disease of children.» The brackets tell you that caries means the same as tooth decay.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. It is about teeth going bad, so caries must be the medical name for that damage. Check by swapping the meaning in: «Tooth decay is the most common long-lasting disease of children» still makes sense, so your guess fits.
explain: Some words belong to one subject. Caries is a formal, medical word, so you will mostly meet it in science, health lessons or at the dentist's. At home, people say tooth decay or cavities.
fact: Caries is tooth decay: the slow damage to teeth that makes holes called cavities.
fact: «Caries» can also mean decay in bone.
fact: Sugar and bacteria on teeth make acid, and the acid causes caries.
fact: Brushing, fluoride and fewer sugary drinks help to prevent caries.
fact: «Dental caries» is the dentist's phrase for tooth decay in the teeth.
exercise: «Tooth decay (dentists call it caries) is the most common long-lasting disease of children.» What does caries mean? | Strong, healthy bone | A sweet, sugary drink | *Tooth decay | A type of toothbrush
exercise: Which word names the holes that caries makes in teeth? | Bacteria | Acid | Fluoride | *Cavities
exercise: Which two things help to prevent caries? | *Brushing and fluoride | Drinking more fizzy sugary drinks | Eating more sweets every day | Leaving sugar on your teeth overnight
test: Dentists say caries. What do people at home usually say instead? | Bone growth | *Tooth decay or cavities | Dental floss | A sugary sweet
test: Which choice gives good ways to prevent caries? | Eating sweets all day long | Skipping the dentist and hoping for the best | *Brushing and fewer sugary drinks | Leaving teeth unbrushed at night
exam: The sentence says tooth decay is almost always what? | Something that happens only to bones | *Something that can be prevented | Something that makes teeth shine | Something that only grown-ups get
